WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.777
A process can be launched with a fixed
executable and safe argument boundaries while

2
00:00:04.857 --> 00:00:07.568
remaining exposed through its surrounding
context.

3
00:00:07.648 --> 00:00:10.479
File paths determine what the utility
reads and writes.

4
00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:14.836
The current working directory can affect
relative paths and automatic discovery of

5
00:00:14.916 --> 00:00:16.844
configuration, plugins, or scripts.

6
00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:20.719
Environment variables can change
executable search, language runtimes,

7
00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:23.630
credentials, proxy behavior, and tool
configuration.

8
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.879
Treat all three as explicit launch inputs.

9
00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:30.176
Prefer server-side identifiers that map to
controlled files over arbitrary paths

10
00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:31.400
submitted by clients.

11
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.817
Place inputs and outputs beneath approved
directories with application-generated

12
00:00:35.897 --> 00:00:37.765
names and appropriate permissions.

13
00:00:37.845 --> 00:00:40.315
When joining a relative name to a base
directory,

14
00:00:40.395 --> 00:00:44.190
normalize and verify containment using
platform-aware path operations;

15
00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.740
a substring check for two dots is not
sufficient.

16
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.771
Consider symbolic links, junctions,
replacement races,

17
00:00:49.851 --> 00:00:51.900
and how the target utility follows them.

18
00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.377
For sensitive workflows, create private
temporary locations and maintain ownership

19
00:00:56.457 --> 00:00:59.831
of opened files rather than relying only
on a preflight path check.

20
00:00:59.911 --> 00:01:03.585
Set the working directory to a known
application-controlled location.

21
00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:05.352
Do not let request data choose it,

22
00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:08.685
and do not assume the web service's
startup directory is stable.

23
00:01:08.765 --> 00:01:13.102
Review the utility for implicit
configuration lookup in that directory and in parent

24
00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:14.447
or user-home locations.

25
00:01:14.527 --> 00:01:18.804
An absolute input path does not neutralize
a hostile working directory when the tool

26
00:01:18.884 --> 00:01:21.776
also discovers plugins or configuration
relative to it.

27
00:01:21.856 --> 00:01:25.711
Minimize the child environment to the
variables it needs instead of blindly

28
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:27.899
forwarding every secret in process.env.

29
00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:32.016
Preserve platform variables genuinely
required for correct process startup,

30
00:01:32.096 --> 00:01:36.071
but select them deliberately and source
their values from trusted deployment

31
00:01:36.151 --> 00:01:36.995
configuration.

32
00:01:37.075 --> 00:01:39.906
Give credentials only to the operation
that needs them,

33
00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:44.384
and avoid placing secrets in command-line
arguments where operating-system process

34
00:01:44.464 --> 00:01:46.150
listings or logs may expose them.

35
00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.760
Explicit paths, a controlled working
directory,

36
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.057
and a purpose-built environment improve
security and make behavior reproducible

37
00:01:53.137 --> 00:01:53.860
across hosts.
